      "side": 1,
      "message": "not for this CL but worth talking about is how git_cache gets to sha256. we maintain a recipe that uploads a bare repo so builds can use those objects instead of cloning. when remote switches to sha256 those builds will break (sha mismatch between bundle built from sha1 and fetch using sha256). right now, builds will wipe and redownload the bundle (broken since they\u0027re built from sha1), but this should self-recover as our bundle-uploader rebuilds with sha256. we have a followup CL tell builds to skip the redownload step if sha mismatch and clone fresh from remote",
